WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:08.320
Now let's see how the database server executed that temporary SQL.

00:08.360 --> 00:13.600
So now let's say that you are as a data analyst, you have created a query and then you say into a temporary

00:13.640 --> 00:14.040
table.

00:14.080 --> 00:16.400
Now the database engine can identify the query.

00:16.440 --> 00:19.120
And first it's going to go and execute the query.

00:19.120 --> 00:21.040
And then it's going to go and execute it.

00:21.040 --> 00:24.400
And maybe you're going to get the data from the table orders.

00:24.400 --> 00:28.440
And after the query is executed the database engine now has the results.

00:28.480 --> 00:29.800
Now two things can happen.

00:29.800 --> 00:35.240
First the database engine is going to go and store the metadata information in the system catalog.

00:35.280 --> 00:41.520
And now the second thing the database engine can create a table, but this time not in the users but

00:41.520 --> 00:43.800
in that temporary storage in the disk.

00:43.800 --> 00:46.080
So the table can live there for a short time.

00:46.120 --> 00:51.160
And now what you can do, you can write multiple SQL queries that are doing maybe multiple analysis

00:51.160 --> 00:52.320
on top of this table.

00:52.520 --> 00:58.200
So each time you select something, the database engine has to go to the temporary storage and fetch

00:58.200 --> 00:59.200
the data from there.

00:59.240 --> 01:04.120
And now once you are finished and let's say you close your client, the session between you and the

01:04.120 --> 01:05.600
database can end.

01:05.640 --> 01:09.800
And now the database can understand, okay, there is no more connection to this user.

01:10.120 --> 01:12.040
And it's going to go and clean up.

01:12.040 --> 01:17.440
Now the temporary storage with any tables that are created from this session.

01:17.440 --> 01:22.800
So that means the database is automatically cleaning up the storage maybe for other sessions.

01:22.800 --> 01:26.280
So this is how the database engine works with the temporary tables.
